sion_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_mcp_writes.py:85-105 `_ack(...)` returns `WriteAckOut.model_validate({\"result\": result, \"push_status\": ..., \"description_warning\": ..., \"cross_session_warning\": ...})` — the ack field is `result`, not `ok`","_mcp_models.py:293-299 WriteAckOut docstring: 'FastMCP already derived {\"result\": <str>} ... result is unchanged' — no `ok` field","_mcp_models.py:499 and :510: the only `ok: bool` fields belong to PlanReviewStatusOut / VerifyCompletionStatusOut (read status models), unrelated to write acks","_mcp_writes.py:488 current declare_no_file_impact returns the bare string 'ok'"],"finding":"The plan's premise that declare_no_file_impact can adopt 'the existing additive ack dict shape so it can include ok and optional cross_session_warning' is not backed by the code: the existing MCP write-ack shape (WriteAckOut, produced by _ack()) exposes a field named 'result' (whose value is 'ok'), not a field named 'ok'. No existing MCP write-ack model carries an 'ok' field (ok:bool exists only on the unrelated PlanReviewStatusOut/VerifyCompletionStatusOut read models at _mcp_models.py:499/510). The plan therefore both mis-describes an 'existing' shape and leaves ambiguous whether it means reuse WriteAckOut (field 'result') or introduce a new shape with an 'ok' field.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5c8f9326a0edbdae","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach bullet 3 ('Change _mcp_writes.declare_no_file_impact ... to the existing additive ack dict shape so it can include ok') and AC line 3/4 ('additive ack object containing ok')","norm_id":"nb857c02484b22308","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer reuses WriteAckOut (which has `result`, not `ok`) and the tests written to AC's `ok` field fail","Implementer invents a new `{ok: bool, cross_session_warning}` model, contradicting the 'existing' wording and diverging from the WriteAckOut pattern 734d established for every other single-ticket write"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Either (a) reuse the existing WriteAckOut via _ack() and reword the ACs to reference `result` (its actual ack field) rather than `ok`, or (b) state explicitly that a NEW ack model with an `ok: bool` field is introduced for declare_no_file_impact and stop describing it as 'the existing additive ack dict shape'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the ack-shape description to name the existing WriteAckOut field `result` (value 'ok') plus `cross_session_warning`, rather than a field literally named `ok`.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_mcp_writes.py:85 `def _ack(result: str = 'ok', ...)` returns WriteAckOut.model_validate({'result': result, 'push_status': ..., 'description_warning': ..., 'cross_session_warning': ...})","_mcp_models.py:301 WriteAckOut declares `result: str`, `push_status`, `description_warning`, `cross_session_warning` — no field named `ok`"],"finding":"The plan describes the additive ack for declare_no_file_impact as an object 'containing ok', but the existing shared ack shape (_ack -> WriteAckOut) exposes a field named 'result' (value 'ok'), not a field literally named 'ok'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f385cc521d333f62b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach bullet 3 / AC line 3 ('additive ack object containing ok')","norm_id":"ne28c1dcd15226657","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer follows the plan literally and looks for/creates an 'ok' key, diverging from the established WriteAckOut ack shape used by the sibling write tools"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword to: 'return the shared WriteAckOut ack ({result, push_status, description_warning, cross_session_warning}) via the existing _ack(...) helper', matching set_file_impact / set_verify_commands.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Clarify